        "<b>Spondylolisthesis</b>: forward slip on lateral view; <b>Meyerding</b> I (up to 25%), II, III, IV (75-100%), then spondyloptosis. Isthmic often L5-S1; degenerative often L4-L5.",
        "<b>Disc terms</b>: bulge (broad), protrusion (base wider), extrusion (fragment wider than base or migrated), sequestration (free fragment).",
        "<b>Asymptomatic findings</b> are common and rise with age; correlate imaging with dermatomes, myotomes, reflexes, and neurodynamic tests.",
        "<b>Spine imaging indicated</b> for red flags, progressive neuro deficit, or when results will guide injection or surgery.",
        "<b>Stroke</b>: non-contrast CT first to exclude <b>hemorrhage</b> (bright); early ischemia often normal on CT. <b>MRI DWI</b> is most sensitive for acute ischemia.",
        "<b>Acute care</b>: check imaging results, BP parameters, and post-thrombolysis precautions before mobilizing."
